title: Let's make all the subsystem experts.
pid: 3d54f315-b39a-4596-a6bd-80a40ab12e3d
body: |2-
  Frequently we will need to ask for a change to a particular system --
  the UI, the renderer, etc. -- and it seems efficient to use a persistent
  team member for such jobs.

  I could be wrong. Maybe the overhead of maintaining persistent agents
  is not worth it. But it seems basically costless, particularly once you
  have introduced a Libby agent who can tend their knowledge without incurring
  your Fable-scale usage rate.

  This also has the advantage that if they get into a pinch, they can talk to you,
  through the graph. (They'll need a way to notify you also.
  Maybe you should just have a watcher looking at all your inboxes.)
